    {
        "text": "The sky after rain is always exceptionally clear."
    },
    {
        "text": "This is one of the rare reasons that Kristen ever steps out of her laboratory."
    },
    {
        "text": "It isn't that she particularly likes the twinkling lights. If conjectures cannot be proven, then they are only self-deceiving lies."
    },
    {
        "text": "Yet lies aren't completely meaningless. Even if a shadow has been twisted thousands of times, it is still cast by something that is real and truthful."
    },
    {
        "text": "Lies exist only to demonstrate one thing\u2014that the truth also exists."
    },
    {
        "text": "It is hidden among these radiant, twinkling stars, and the sky also isn't as far as it seems."
    },
    {
        "text": "When she reaches her hand out, she will surely be able to touch it\u2014"
    },
    {
        "text": "The only truth that has been suffocating the people from up above for thousands of years."
    },
